e: Wednesday, March 18th, 2026 — 8:10 PM (Asia/Shanghai) / 2026-03-18 12:10 UTC\"\n        }\n      ],\n      \"timestamp\": 1773835832742\n    },\n    {\n      \"role\": \"assistant\",\n      \"content\": [\n        {\n          \"type\": \"thinking\",\n          \"thinking\": \"**Inspecting memory files**\\n\\nI need to comply with the session startup, which might already have some context loaded. The instructions say I should read the required files before responding. Specifically, I need to check the SOUL USER memory for today and yesterday, as well as the MEMORY file since it's a direct chat. I might also need to create the today file if it's not there. Let's take a closer look at those memory files.\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_slMbLkmHmPEyuYgijiWcOlpw|fc_0099dfe7541593d80169ba9640e6d88191a71ccfcea300b894\",\n          \"name\": \"read\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"file_path\": \"/root/.openclaw/workspace/SOUL.md\"\n          },\n          \"partialJson\": \"{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/SOUL.md\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_c5buRaQggXpyh2vcvjHVteCr|fc_0099dfe7541593d80169ba9640e6e48191a48655678fca99ac\",\n          \"name\": \"read\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"file_path\": \"/root/.openclaw/workspace/USER.md\"\n          },\n          \"partialJson\": \"{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/USER.md\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"call_Mgesvqix8CRwYyWU9SI8kfMf|fc_0099dfe7541593d80169ba9640e6ec8191a39da00bf02c60bb\",\n          \"name\": \"read\",\n          \"arguments\": {\n            \"file_path\": \"/root/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md\"\n          },\n          \"partialJson\": \"{\\\"file_path\\\":\\\"/root/.openclaw/workspace/MEMORY.md\\\"}\"\n        },\n        {\n          \"type\": \"toolCall\",\n          \"id\": \"cal